.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis
.Nd post-quantum signatures, KEMs, hashes and sealed capsules in C11
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Bd -literal
cc prog.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs noqtis)

find_package(noqtis CONFIG REQUIRED)        # CMake
target_link_libraries(prog PRIVATE noqtis::noqtis)
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
noqtis is a library in ISO C11 with no run-time dependencies.
It provides the NIST post-quantum standards, byte-identical to their test
vectors, and on top of them capsules: folders whose exact files are
recorded, signed and checked.
.Bl -tag -width "nqseal(3)"
.It Xr nqsign 3
ML-DSA (FIPS 204) and SLH-DSA (FIPS 205): key generation, signing (pure,
with a context, and pre-hash) and verification:
.Fn nqskg ,
.Fn nqskgd ,
.Fn nqsign ,
.Fn nqsignd ,
.Fn nqvrfy ,
.Fn nqssize ,
.Fn nqsname ,
.Fn nqsfind .
.It Xr nqenc 3
ML-KEM (FIPS 203) and HQC:
.Fn nqkkg ,
.Fn nqkkgd ,
.Fn nqenc ,
.Fn nqencd ,
.Fn nqdec ,
.Fn nqksize ,
.Fn nqkname ,
.Fn nqkfind .
.It Xr nqhash 3
SHA-2, SHA-3, SHAKE and HMAC:
.Fn nqhash ,
.Fn nqhini ,
.Fn nqhupd ,
.Fn nqhfin ,
.Fn nqhlen ,
.Fn nqhmac .
.It Xr nqseal 3
Seal a folder.
.It Xr nqchk 3
Check a capsule.
.It Xr nqchkt 3
Check a capsule and its RFC 3161 timestamp.
.It Xr nqtsput 3
Timestamp a seal:
.Fn nqtsreq ,
.Fn nqtsput .
.It Xr nqrep 3
Read the check report:
.Fn nqrepn ,
.Fn nqrepi ,
.Fn nqrepfree .
.It Xr nqrand 3
The operating system's random source.
.It Xr nqwipe 3
Erase secrets.
.It Xr nqcteq 3
Constant-time comparison.
.It Xr nqsetal 3
The allocation hook.
.It Xr nqerr 3
Error codes and texts,
.Fn nqver .
.El
.Ss Conventions
.Bl -bullet
.It
Every function that can fail returns
.Vt int :
.Dv NQOK
(0) or a negative
.Dv NQE*
code
.Pq Xr nqerr 3 .
A failed verification is
.Er NQEVRFY ,
never
.Dv NQOK .
.It
Keys, signatures and ciphertexts are byte strings in the encodings the
standards define.
Their sizes are fixed per algorithm and available at run time from
.Fn nqssize
and
.Fn nqksize .
.It
The caller allocates every output buffer and passes its length.
A function never writes past that length, and returns
.Er NQEBUF
when it is too small.
.It
Secrets are wiped with
.Fn nqwipe
before a function returns, on every path.
Operations on secret data run in constant time.
.It
Randomness comes from
.Fn nqrand
unless a caller passes the standard's seed or randomness through a
.Ql d
variant
.Pf ( Fn nqskgd ,
.Fn nqsignd ,
.Fn nqkkgd ,
.Fn nqencd ) ,
which exist for the test vectors.
.It
The algorithm code never allocates.
The capsule layer allocates through the hook of
.Fn nqsetal .
.It
Paths are UTF-8 on every operating system.
.It
The functions are thread safe, except
.Fn nqsetal ,
as long as threads do not share an
.Vt nqhctx ,
an
.Vt nqrep
being freed, or a capsule folder being sealed.
.El
.Ss Building
The library builds with CMake
.Pq Ql cmake -S . -B build && cmake --build build ,
static by default,
.Fl DNQSHARED=ON
for shared.
A shared build exports only the public functions; on Windows, programs
that use the DLL define
.Dv NQDLL
(the CMake package and
.Pa noqtis.pc
do it).
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa include/noqtis.h
the public header
.It Pa lib/libnoqtis.a , lib/libnoqtis.so.0
the library
.It Pa lib/pkgconfig/noqtis.pc
the pkg-config file
.It Pa lib/cmake/noqtis/
the CMake package
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <noqtis.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
  printf("noqtis %s\en", nqver());
  return 0;
}
.Ed
.Pp
More in
.Pa docs/examples
of the source tree; every one is compiled and run in CI.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
.Sh STANDARDS
FIPS 180-4, FIPS 198-1, FIPS 202, FIPS 203, FIPS 204, FIPS 205,
SP 800-90A (HMAC_DRBG, internal), HQC version 5.0.0, RFC 3161, RFC 8785.
.Sh CAVEATS
noqtis has not had an external security audit.
